 "sq": [
  {
   "_id": 17429,
   "ANSWER": "<p data-end=\"1122\" data-start=\"1062\">Control signals are <strong data-end=\"353\" data-start=\"335\">binary signals</strong> generated by the <strong data-end=\"387\" data-start=\"371\">control unit</strong> to direct the operations of the processor. These signals coordinate the flow of data among the CPU, memory, and I/O devices during instruction execution. Control signals determine what actions the hardware components should take, such as <strong data-end=\"649\" data-start=\"626\">reading from memory</strong>, <strong data-end=\"676\" data-start=\"651\">writing to a register</strong>, <strong data-end=\"698\" data-start=\"678\">enabling the ALU</strong>, or <strong data-end=\"739\" data-start=\"703\">incrementing the program counter</strong>. They are essential in managing the <strong data-end=\"800\" data-start=\"776\">fetch-decode-execute</strong> cycle and ensure that every operation happens in the correct sequence and timing.</p>\n",
   "COURSE_CODE": "21CSS201T",
   "LEVEL": 2,
   "OUTCOMES": [
    "PLO1",
    "PLO14"
   ],
   "QUESTION_DESC": "<p>What are control signals in a computer system?</p>\n",
   "SESSION_ID": 408,
   "TYPE": "sq",
   "key": 17429
  },
  {
   "_id": 17430,
   "ANSWER": "<p data-end=\"1122\" data-start=\"1062\">In a <strong data-end=\"1692\" data-start=\"1666\">hardwired control unit</strong>, control signals are generated using <strong data-end=\"1762\" data-start=\"1730\">combinational logic circuits</strong> based on the <strong data-end=\"1805\" data-start=\"1776\">opcode of the instruction</strong> and <strong data-end=\"1828\" data-start=\"1810\">timing signals</strong>. The instruction is first decoded using a <strong data-end=\"1882\" data-start=\"1871\">decoder</strong>, which determines which operation is needed. Then, using logic gates and flip-flops, the corresponding control signals are generated at specific clock cycles. For example, during an ADD instruction, the ALU enable and register select signals are activated. Since everything is implemented in hardware, the signal generation is very fast but <strong data-end=\"2251\" data-start=\"2224\">not easily programmable</strong>.</p>\n",
   "COURSE_CODE": "21CSS201T",
   "LEVEL": 3,
   "OUTCOMES": [
    "PLO1",
    "PLO14"
   ],
   "QUESTION_DESC": "<p>How are control signals generated in a hardwired control unit?</p>\n",
   "SESSION_ID": 408,
   "TYPE": "sq",
   "key": 17430
  }
 ],
 "lq": [
  {
   "_id": 17579,
   "ANSWER": "<p data-end=\"3992\" data-start=\"3802\">Let us analyze the <strong data-end=\"3867\" data-start=\"3835\">execution of the instruction</strong> <code data-end=\"3880\" data-start=\"3868\">ADD R1, R2</code> in a micro-programmed control unit, assuming it adds the content of <code data-end=\"3953\" data-start=\"3949\">R2</code> to <code data-end=\"3961\" data-start=\"3957\">R1</code> and stores the result in <code data-end=\"3991\" data-start=\"3987\">R1</code>.</p>\n\n<h4 data-end=\"4038\" data-start=\"3994\"><strong data-end=\"4038\" data-start=\"3999\">Steps in Microprogrammed Execution:</strong></h4>\n\n<ol data-end=\"4758\" data-start=\"4040\">\n\t<li data-end=\"4197\" data-start=\"4040\">\n\t<p data-end=\"4082\" data-start=\"4043\"><strong data-end=\"4082\" data-start=\"4043\">Instruction Fetch (Common Routine):</strong></p>\n\n\t<ul data-end=\"4197\" data-start=\"4086\">\n\t\t<li data-end=\"4118\" data-start=\"4086\">\n\t\t<p data-end=\"4118\" data-start=\"4088\">Fetch instruction from memory.</p>\n\t\t</li>\n\t\t<li data-end=\"4197\" data-start=\"4122\">\n\t\t<p data-end=\"4142\" data-start=\"4124\">Microinstructions:</p>\n\n\t\t<ul data-end=\"4197\" data-start=\"4148\">\n\t\t\t<li data-end=\"4166\" data-start=\"4148\">\n\t\t\t<p data-end=\"4166\" data-start=\"4150\"><code data-end=\"4166\" data-start=\"4150\">PC &rarr; MAR; Read</code></p>\n\t\t\t</li>\n\t\t\t<li data-end=\"4197\" data-start=\"4172\">\n\t\t\t<p data-end=\"4197\" data-start=\"4174\"><code data-end=\"4197\" data-start=\"4174\">MDR &rarr; IR; PC = PC + 1</code></p>\n\t\t\t</li>\n\t\t</ul>\n\t\t</li>\n\t</ul>\n\t</li>\n\t<li data-end=\"4369\" data-start=\"4199\">\n\t<p data-end=\"4225\" data-start=\"4202\"><strong data-end=\"4225\" data-start=\"4202\">Instruction Decode:</strong></p>\n\n\t<ul data-end=\"4369\" data-start=\"4229\">\n\t\t<li data-end=\"4345\" data-start=\"4229\">\n\t\t<p data-end=\"4345\" data-start=\"4231\">The opcode of the instruction is decoded to locate the starting address of the microprogram in <strong data-end=\"4344\" data-start=\"4326\">control memory</strong>.</p>\n\t\t</li>\n\t\t<li data-end=\"4369\" data-start=\"4349\">\n\t\t<p data-end=\"4369\" data-start=\"4351\"><code data-end=\"4369\" data-start=\"4351\">IR(opcode) &rarr; CAR</code></p>\n\t\t</li>\n\t</ul>\n\t</li>\n\t<li data-end=\"4628\" data-start=\"4371\">\n\t<p data-end=\"4399\" data-start=\"4374\"><strong data-end=\"4399\" data-start=\"4374\">Execute <code data-end=\"4396\" data-start=\"4384\">ADD R1, R2</code>:</strong></p>\n\n\t<ul data-end=\"4628\" data-start=\"4403\">\n\t\t<li data-end=\"4468\" data-start=\"4403\">\n\t\t<p data-end=\"4426\" data-start=\"4405\">Microinstruction 1:</p>\n\n\t\t<ul data-end=\"4468\" data-start=\"4432\">\n\t\t\t<li data-end=\"4468\" data-start=\"4432\">\n\t\t\t<p data-end=\"4468\" data-start=\"4434\"><code data-end=\"4447\" data-start=\"4434\">R1 &rarr; Temp A</code> (load first operand)</p>\n\t\t\t</li>\n\t\t</ul>\n\t\t</li>\n\t\t<li data-end=\"4538\" data-start=\"4472\">\n\t\t<p data-end=\"4495\" data-start=\"4474\">Microinstruction 2:</p>\n\n\t\t<ul data-end=\"4538\" data-start=\"4501\">\n\t\t\t<li data-end=\"4538\" data-start=\"4501\">\n\t\t\t<p data-end=\"4538\" data-start=\"4503\"><code data-end=\"4516\" data-start=\"4503\">R2 &rarr; Temp B</code> (load second operand)</p>\n\t\t\t</li>\n\t\t</ul>\n\t\t</li>\n\t\t<li data-end=\"4628\" data-start=\"4542\">\n\t\t<p data-end=\"4565\" data-start=\"4544\">Microinstruction 3:</p>\n\n\t\t<ul data-end=\"4628\" data-start=\"4571\">\n\t\t\t<li data-end=\"4628\" data-start=\"4571\">\n\t\t\t<p data-end=\"4628\" data-start=\"4573\"><code data-end=\"4599\" data-start=\"4573\">ALU = A + B; Result &rarr; R1</code> (perform addition and store)</p>\n\t\t\t</li>\n\t\t</ul>\n\t\t</li>\n\t</ul>\n\t</li>\n\t<li data-end=\"4758\" data-start=\"4630\">\n\t<p data-end=\"4656\" data-start=\"4633\"><strong data-end=\"4656\" data-start=\"4633\">End of Instruction:</strong></p>\n\n\t<ul data-end=\"4758\" data-start=\"4660\">\n\t\t<li data-end=\"4758\" data-start=\"4660\">\n\t\t<p data-end=\"4758\" data-start=\"4662\">A microinstruction signals <strong data-end=\"4708\" data-start=\"4689\">end-of-sequence</strong>, returning control to fetch the next instruction.</p>\n\t\t</li>\n\t</ul>\n\t</li>\n</ol>\n\n<h4 data-end=\"4810\" data-start=\"4760\"><strong data-end=\"4810\" data-start=\"4765\">Control Signals in Each Microinstruction:</strong></h4>\n\n<ul data-end=\"4938\" data-start=\"4811\">\n\t<li data-end=\"4938\" data-start=\"4811\">\n\t<p data-end=\"4938\" data-start=\"4813\">Selected using <strong data-end=\"4846\" data-start=\"4828\">control fields</strong> in each microinstruction, which activate ALU, register selectors, buses, and write enables.</p>\n\t</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h4 data-end=\"4960\" data-start=\"4940\"><strong data-end=\"4960\" data-start=\"4945\">Advantages:</strong></h4>\n\n<ul data-end=\"5048\" data-start=\"4961\">\n\t<li data-end=\"4989\" data-start=\"4961\">\n\t<p data-end=\"4989\" data-start=\"4963\">Easy to design and extend.</p>\n\t</li>\n\t<li data-end=\"5048\" data-start=\"4990\">\n\t<p data-end=\"5048\" data-start=\"4992\">Supports complex instructions without changing hardware.</p>\n\t</li>\n</ul>\n\n<p data-end=\"5234\" data-start=\"5050\">This example shows how a simple instruction is broken into smaller micro-operations and executed through sequenced <strong data-end=\"5186\" data-start=\"5165\">microinstructions</strong>, with each generating specific control signals.</p>\n",
   "COURSE_CODE": "21CSS201T",
   "LEVEL": 3,
   "OUTCOMES": [
    "PLO1",
    "PLO14"
   ],
   "QUESTION_DESC": "<p>Apply the concept of micro-programmed control to explain how an instruction like <code data-end=\"3753\" data-start=\"3741\">ADD R1, R2</code> is executed.</p>\n",
   "SESSION_ID": 408,
   "TYPE": "lq",
   "key": 17579
  }
 ]
